            notes: "The population of the hominin of the same name: groups of five to twenty-five that forage over the savanna–woodland and along the gallery forests by day, never far from water and the trees they sleep in. Rare and wary; the leopard, the big cats, the hyenas, the crocodiles and the crowned eagle take them.",
